jobs.description:
The Domus Foundation , a Valais institution for psychosocial rehabilitation, supports adults facing significant mental health challenges.
 Nearly 150 collaborators are committed there with conviction and professionalism.
 Our vision: self-determination for everyone, a solution-focused approach, and professional practices marked by kindness and responsibility .
 We are looking for our Ardon residence a:

Social and Educational Assistant at 75%

from 1 January 2027 or as agreed

We offer you to

• ensure the support of beneficiaries within the Ardon Residence in their daily life activities from a psychosocial rehabilitation perspective based on self-determination;

• support residents in their individual projects and goals;

• collaborate interprofessionally with social workers, nurses, ASSC, day centres and workshops.

We offer you

• to join a foundation guided by participative management, a positive dynamic and a strong spirit of openness;

• to integrate into an institution concerned with the well-being of everyone and the teams where listening, collaboration, mutual aid and friendliness are cultivated;

• to make your place in a structure that regularly runs many projects to which everyone can contribute;

• to benefit from a pleasant working environment, with annually planned team schedules, and good social and salary conditions;

• continuous training every year through our Agir Ensemble training catalogue.

Your profile

• you hold a CFC as a social and educational assistant or an equivalent qualification;

• you have confirmed work experience in the field of psychiatry or social work;

• with a very good sense of organisation, you enjoy working in a team and being able to take on responsibilities;

• you are proficient with common IT tools (MS Office);

• holder of a driving licence, you have a private vehicle.

Interested?
 Further information can be obtained at 027 205 75 00. Please send us your complete application with CV, photo, cover letter, diplomas and work certificates by 28 October 2026. Applications will be treated confidentially.

